sec.p:
Two wheat populations were used in this study to investigate the effect of genotyping errors on QTL mapping. The first population was Yangxiaomai × Zhongyou 9507 F6 RILs (YZ) with population size of 193 [24–26], planted in Beijing and Shijiazhuang during 2011 and 2012, Gaoyi during 2018 and 2020, Xinxiang during 2019 and 2021. Five traits were measured, i.e., grain number per spike (GNS), thousand grain weight (TGW), grain length (GL), grain width (GW), and pre-harvest sprouting (PHS). The second population was Jingshuang 16 × Bainong 64 F6 RILs (JB) with population size of 181 [27], planted in Beijing, Gaoyi and Shijiazhuang from 2019 to 2020. Plant height (PH) was measured. Heritability and BLUE (best linear unbiased estimation) values of the traits was calculated across environments by the AOV functionality in software package QTL IciMapping V4.2 [20]. Two levels of broad-sense heritability were calculated. The formula for plot level heritability was \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
